From: PyDevices usbif
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shared/tinyusb: allow a user C module to vary the built-in
 configuration descriptor at runtime

Purpose: a class contributed by a user C module should not be advertised to
the host unless the application has asked for it. A board that always
enumerates as a sound card is not merely untidy -- the host may make it the
default audio device, route system audio to it, and stall its audio engine
when nothing on the board is draining the stream. Observed on Windows: the
desktop backed up, including keyboard input, until the default was changed.

Two weak hooks, both defaulting to today's compile-time behaviour, so a build
without such a module is bit-for-bit unchanged:

  mp_usbd_builtin_desc_cfg_get()  substitutes the built-in configuration
                                  descriptor
  mp_usbd_builtin_itf_max()       the matching interface count, which
                                  runtime_dev_open() uses to decide which
                                  interfaces belong to built-in drivers

Both are needed together: varying the descriptor without varying the bound
would leave runtime_dev_open declining interfaces that are no longer built-in,
so a Python-defined interface occupying that number would be claimed by
nobody.

Provenance: written for usbif Phase 4, 2026-08-29.
Upstream-version range: authored against v1.28.0.
Order: applies after 0001 and 0002.
Test: with a module that enables its class only on request, the board
enumerates as plain CDC until asked and as a composite device afterwards, and
the host's default-device selection follows.

--- a/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd.h
+++ b/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd.h
@@ -101,6 +101,15 @@
     MICROPY_HW_USB_EXT_DESC_CFG_LEN           \
     )
 
+// A user C module contributing built-in interfaces may need to vary them at
+// runtime -- a class the application has not asked for should not be
+// advertised to the host. These weak hooks let it substitute the built-in
+// configuration descriptor and the interface count that goes with it; the
+// defaults return the compile-time values, so a build without such a module
+// behaves exactly as before.
+const uint8_t *mp_usbd_builtin_desc_cfg_get(void);
+uint8_t mp_usbd_builtin_itf_max(void);
+
 // Built-in USB device and configuration descriptor values
 extern const tusb_desc_device_t mp_usbd_builtin_desc_dev;
 extern const uint8_t mp_usbd_builtin_desc_cfg[MP_USBD_BUILTIN_DESC_CFG_LEN];
--- a/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd_runtime.c
+++ b/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd_runtime.c
@@ -123,7 +123,17 @@
     if (usbd) {
         result = usbd_get_buffer_in_cb(usbd->desc_cfg, MP_BUFFER_READ);
     }
-    return result ? result : &mp_usbd_builtin_desc_cfg;
+    return result ? result : mp_usbd_builtin_desc_cfg_get();
+}
+
+// Defaults: the compile-time built-in descriptor and its interface count. A
+// user C module may override either.
+MP_WEAK const uint8_t *mp_usbd_builtin_desc_cfg_get(void) {
+    return mp_usbd_builtin_desc_cfg;
+}
+
+MP_WEAK uint8_t mp_usbd_builtin_itf_max(void) {
+    return USBD_ITF_BUILTIN_MAX;
 }
 
 const char *mp_usbd_runtime_string_cb(uint8_t index) {
@@ -270,7 +280,7 @@
 
     // If TinyUSB built-in drivers are enabled, don't claim any interface in the built-in range
     #if USBD_ITF_BUILTIN_MAX > 0
-    if (mp_usb_device_builtin_enabled(usbd) && itf_desc->bInterfaceNumber < USBD_ITF_BUILTIN_MAX) {
+    if (mp_usb_device_builtin_enabled(usbd) && itf_desc->bInterfaceNumber < mp_usbd_builtin_itf_max()) {
         return 0;
     }
     #endif
